DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260908T183000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Girls Soccer vs Marblehead (T 2–2)
LOCATION:Dr. Deering Stadium\, Danvers
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nFinal: Danvers 2\, Marblehead 2\nThe F
 alcons twice came back from a goal down in the first half of the season op
 ener but couldn't find a winner despite a 20–7 edge in shots. Mia St. Pi
 erre scored from a tough angle and Emma Sutherland got the second equalize
 r.\nSchedule and results: https://danversfalconsathletics.org/soccer/sched
 ule.html?team=girls
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/soccer/schedule.html?team=girls
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:golf-6@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260909T150000
DURATION:PT3H
SUMMARY:Danvers Golf vs Masconomet (L 33–39)
LOCATION:Wenham Country Club\, Wenham
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nFinal: Danvers 33\, Masconomet 39\nWes
  Maylor\, Cole Andrews and Austin Patuto all won their matches in the home
  opener\, but Masconomet took it by six points behind a 2-under 32 from Br
 endan O'Connor.\nSchedule and results: https://danversfalconsathletics.org
 /golf/schedule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/golf/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cross-country-1@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260909T160000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Cross Country vs Beverly
LOCATION:Danvers High School
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nBoys: lost 31–24\nGirls: lost 32–2
 6\nOpening day against a Northeastern Conference rival. Marcus Morais ran 
 17:54 for second in the boys race — three seconds behind the winner — 
 and Grace Conklin (19:30) and Madyson Danish (20:47) went 2–3 in the gir
 ls race\, but Beverly's depth took both meets.\nSchedule and results: http
 s://danversfalconsathletics.org/cross-country/schedule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/cross-country/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:volleyball-2@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260909T171500
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Volleyball at Triton (W 3–0)
LOCATION:Triton Regional HS\, Byfield
DESCRIPTION:Non-league\nFinal: Danvers 3\, Triton 0\nDanvers served its way
  to Sarah Griffin's first win with 19 aces\, six from Lauren Garofalo and 
 five from Hadley Brown. Gabrielle Lindeman had seven kills and 12 digs\, a
 nd setters Hannah Tersolo and Lila Osborne each handed out 11 assists.\nSc
 hedule and results: https://danversfalconsathletics.org/volleyball/schedul
 e.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/volleyball/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
