UID:girls-soccer-15@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261019T163000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Girls Soccer at Salem (L 1–2)
LOCATION:Bertram Field\, Salem
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nFinal: Danvers 1\, Salem 2\nMia St. Pi
 erre scored with eight minutes to go\, but Danvers couldn't find the equal
 izer. A long-range strike by Jackie Fritz held up as the winner\, and Sale
 m beat Danvers for the first time in close to 20 years.\nSchedule and resu
 lts: https://danversfalconsathletics.org/soccer/schedule.html?team=girls
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/soccer/schedule.html?team=girls
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:boys-soccer-14@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261019T173000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Boys Soccer vs Salem (L 0–2)
LOCATION:Dr. Deering Stadium\, Danvers
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nFinal: Danvers 0\, Salem 2\nA scoreles
 s first half gave way to two second-half goals from Salem senior captain H
 enry Beauparlant.\nSchedule and results: https://danversfalconsathletics.o
 rg/soccer/schedule.html?team=boys
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/soccer/schedule.html?team=boys
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:volleyball-16@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261019T173000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Volleyball at Beverly (L 2–3)
LOCATION:Beverly High School
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nFinal: Danvers 2\, Beverly 3\nDanvers 
 came back from nine points down to win a 29–27 first set and forced a fi
 fth after dropping the next two\, but Beverly pulled away late in the deci
 ding set to split the rivalry series. Lauren Garofalo had nine kills\, thr
 ee aces and 24 digs\, Brooke Bernard seven kills and two blocks\, and Kend
 all Murphy four aces.\nSchedule and results: https://danversfalconsathleti
 cs.org/volleyball/schedule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/volleyball/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:golf-19@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261020T090000
DURATION:PT5H
SUMMARY:Danvers Golf: Division 2 North Sectional (11th of 15)
LOCATION:Bradford Country Club\, Haverhill
DESCRIPTION:MIAA tournament\nFinished 11th of 15 with 348 (+64)\nIn the las
 t MIAA sectional before the state switches formats in 2027\, the Falcons p
 laced 11th of 15 teams at Bradford. Junior Wes Maylor led Danvers with a 9
 -over 81. Masconomet won with 294\, and Newburyport and Milton took the ot
 her two spots in the state final.\nSchedule and results: https://danversfa
 lconsathletics.org/golf/schedule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/golf/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:field-hockey-15@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261020T190000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Field Hockey at Saugus (W 6–2)
LOCATION:Serino Field\, Saugus
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nFinal: Danvers 6\, Saugus 2\nThe Falco
 ns scored six times under the lights at Serino Field to sweep the season s
 eries with Saugus\, getting back above .500 overall and to .500 in the con
 ference.\nSchedule and results: https://danversfalconsathletics.org/field-
 hockey/schedule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/field-hockey/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:golf-18@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261021T090000
DURATION:PT5H
SUMMARY:Danvers Golf: NEC Open (4th of 10)
LOCATION:Tedesco Country Club\, Marblehead
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference tournament\nFinished 4th of 10 with 179
  (+39)\nCold temperatures\, swirling winds and lightning-fast greens made 
 Tedesco play tough at the conference's season-ending tournament. Danvers f
 inished fourth of 10 teams with a 179\, one shot ahead of Swampscott\, and
  junior Ben Campbell tied for seventh individually with a 15-over 85. Marb
 lehead won the team title with 163 and Tyler Forbes was the medalist with 
 a 79.\nSchedule and results: https://danversfalconsathletics.org/golf/sche
 dule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/golf/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
